WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Paris, 1833.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:07.760
A student called Frédéric Ozanam and his
friends start a society to serve people

3
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.830
in need.

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.950
Today its local groups still
meet, often in a parish.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.370
In 1962, the bishops of England
and Wales founded CAFOD,

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.170
to work with local partners overseas.

7
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.530
So what does love your neighbour look
like on a Tuesday night in your town,

8
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.310
and across the world?

9
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.710
In this mission, you'll follow help
from a parish to communities far away,

10
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.420
and find out why.

11
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:37.080
Then you'll weigh up a claim: that
supporting a charity is the best way to love

12
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.240
your neighbour.

13
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.530
Your mission: find out what
love of neighbour looks like,

14
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.730
next door and across the world.
